Well, the opinion of the guys who wrote the game is clearly different from
yours -- that's why it deletes save files when you load the character.
And the opinion of the vast majority of those who play is different from
yours, because we respect the DevTeam's wishes and we enjoy the game they
designed (rather than our own modified "easy" version.)

So what you're doing is, clearly, cheating.

That said, cheating in a video game is not morally wrong (unless you're
playing for money, or on someone else's server.)  As you said:

> NetHack is free.  My copy is mine, therefore I can do with it as I
please.
> If I want to change the code to make all gnomes zap themselves with
wands
> of death, I can do so.

And of course you can.  That doesn't mean it's not cheating, it just means
it's ok if you do so.  If you want to play nethack-with-saves, go for
it -- or if you want to play nethack-with-suicide-gnomes, go for it.  Or
if you want to go play Quake, or Diablo, or Soccer, go for it.  But it's
not going to make most players better if they cheat as a habit... and if
you do beat the game by cheating, don't come on here and brag to us about
it.  People who use patches -- even very minor ones -- will say so when
they post an ascension, to make it clear exactly what game they beat.  If
you beat it by savescumming, don't try to pass it off as a legitimate
victory -- the devteam certainly didn't intend it, so if you do it, you
didn't beat the same game as the rest of us have.

Now, as I said before, there's nothing wrong with cheating.  What's wrong,
and why people are responding so angrily to you, is that you're cheating
and pretending you're not -- it's disrespectful to those of us who've beat
the game legitimately to pretend that beating it using savescums is just
as big of an accomplishment.

Now, to respond to your earlier point: I convinced my wife to savescum
once, and it helped her game tremendously.  It is advice I'd give to
people who are badly stuck -- but not in the way you gave it.  Don't tell
people to make a habit of savescumming -- that will not make them better.
No, rather, do like my wife did -- use savescums the same way you'd use
explore mode: to look at the late game, to try different approaches to
similar problems, and to learn what sort of things you need to be planning
for.  If you do this, you really can improve your game -- but only if you
do it with the intent of improving your game, and only if you understand
what you're doing.  If you savescum to make the game easier, all you'll do
is train yourself to beat an easier game -- which is not useful.



